<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suzdal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suzdal is a small town in Vladimir Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the Kamenka river. First recorded in 1024, it became the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-dolgoruky">Yuri Dolgoruky</a> in the 12th century, giving its name to the principality of Rostov-Suzdal and later Vladimir-Suzdal. After political power moved to Vladimir and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> it remained a religious centre full of monasteries, and its kremlin and churches are a World Heritage site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suzdal.jpg" alt="Suzdal" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ludvig14 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SuzdalPanoramaC_9345.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
